Step 3 — Create the Mango Index
click:Run A Query with Mango → then look for the Index option. →Click Manage Indexes. Then create a JSON index on marks:

Query 2 — Find a student by rollno 101
{
"selector": { "roll_no": 101
}
}

Query 2 — Students who scored more than 400
{
"selector": {
"marks": {
"$gt": 400
}
}
}

Query 3 — CS students with marks > 400

{
"selector": { "course": "CS", "marks": {
"$gt": 400
}
}
}

Query 4 — CS OR marks > 400

{
"selector": {
"$or": [
{
"course": "CS"
},
{
"marks": {
"$gt": 400
}
}
]
}
}

Query 5 — Sort students by marks descending

{
"selector": {}, "sort": [
{
"marks": "desc"
}
]
}

Query 6 — CS students, roll number descending, only course and roll_no
Create roll number index: Click Manage Indexes → create this:

{
"index": {
"fields": [ "roll_no"
]
},
"name": "rollno-index",
"type": "json"
}

Now run Query 6
{
"selector": {
"course": "CS"
},
"fields": [
"course", "roll_no"
],
"sort": [
{
"roll_no": "desc"
}
]
}
